arm64: dts: h713: add pwm-backlight on PWM2/PB4 for panel dimming

The projector panel's backlight comes on (PB5 enables the rail) but sits at a
fixed, dim, power-on-default level and is not yet brightness-controllable under
mainline. An earlier bench note concluded "a running 25 kHz PWM on PB4 changed
brightness not at all, so PB4/PWM2 is not the control" -- but the captured
stock vendor DTB says otherwise, from three independent directions:

  - the stock tvtop panel block sets panel_pwm_ch = 2 (PB4), panel_pwm_freq =
    25000 (25 kHz, period 40000 ns), panel_backlight = 75 on a 0..100 duty
    scale (panel_pwm_min = 0, panel_pwm_max = 100, panel_pwm_pol = 0);
  - stock U-Boot fastlogo drives exactly this channel: pwm_request(2,
    "fastlogo"); the boot log prints "Display fastlogo finish!";
  - the vendor Linux port ships a working backlight-class driver that dims via
    PWM channel 2 and treats PB5 purely as an on/off enable.

So PB4/PWM2 IS the stock dimmer. The most likely reason poking it in isolation
did nothing: this is a serially-programmed LED panel whose drive currents
(panel_de_current, panel_*_data_current) and PWM-dim acceptance are configured
over the panel's SPI link by fastlogo before Linux runs. On the bench that init
never happens, so the panel ignores the PWM pin and stays at its default level.
This patch does not resolve that; it wires the dimmer the mainline way so the
hypothesis can be tested cleanly: boot, then sweep
/sys/class/backlight/backlight/brightness (0..100) with a scope/DMM on PB4. If
brightness tracks duty, the earlier negative was a test artifact and this node
is the end state. If a full 0..100 sweep still does nothing while PB4 provably
carries the signal, the panel serial-init gate is confirmed and the work moves
to extracting fastlogo's panel init sequence.

Model it as a standard pwm-backlight on &pwm channel 2 (PB4), 40000 ns / 25
kHz, with a linear 0..100 brightness scale (five anchors interpolated in steps
of 25) and the stock default of 75. PB5 (panel_bl_en) is shared with
cooling-fan power and is held high by fan_power_hog; it is deliberately NOT
wired as enable-gpios here, because driving PB5 low to "blank" the backlight
would also cut the fan. This node varies PWM duty only; the panel rail stays
powered by the hog. Polarity uses the stock vendor-DTB value (normal, flag 0);
the board's tvtop_config carries panel_pwm_pol = 1, so if a sweep reads
inverted, flip the third pwms cell to PWM_POLARITY_INVERTED.

CONFIG_BACKLIGHT_PWM and CONFIG_PWM_SUN8I are already enabled, and the H713 PWM
controller registers all eight channels, so the node binds without further
kernel changes. The ge2d node also references <&pwm 2 ...> for future display
work, but "trix,ge2d" has no mainline driver, so only pwm-backlight actually
claims the channel at runtime -- no consumer conflict.
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -1550,6 +1550,36 @@
 		status = "okay";
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Panel backlight dimming (bench bring-up).
+	 *
+	 * Brightness input is PWM channel 2 on PB4 -- the stock dimmer. The
+	 * vendor DTB sets panel_pwm_ch = 2 at 25 kHz (period 40000 ns) on a
+	 * 0..100 duty scale (see tvtop_config below), and stock U-Boot fastlogo
+	 * drives it with pwm_request(2, "fastlogo"). Model it as a standard
+	 * pwm-backlight so brightness is controllable from
+	 * /sys/class/backlight/backlight/brightness for evaluation.
+	 *
+	 * PB5 (panel_bl_en) is shared with cooling-fan power and is held high by
+	 * fan_power_hog; it must never be driven low (that cuts the fan). It is
+	 * therefore deliberately NOT wired here as enable-gpios -- this node
+	 * varies PWM duty only, and the panel stays powered by the hog.
+	 *
+	 * Polarity is the stock vendor-DTB value (normal, flag 0). If a duty
+	 * sweep reads inverted, change the third pwms cell to
+	 * PWM_POLARITY_INVERTED (and #include dt-bindings/pwm/pwm.h) to match
+	 * tvtop_config's panel_pwm_pol = 1.
+	 */
+	backlight: backlight {
+		compatible = "pwm-backlight";
+		pwms = <&pwm 2 40000 0>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&pwm2_pins>;
+		brightness-levels = <0 25 50 75 100>;
+		num-interpolated-steps = <25>;
+		default-brightness-level = <75>;
+	};
+
 		/*
 		 * U-Boot: early GPIO init.
 		 * Sets PB3 as output LOW during boot.
